  "narrative": {
    "intro": "AmerisourceBergen Drug obligated $5.1B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. AmerisourceBergen Drug won 328,437 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $15.6K. Obligations fell 31.2% year over year. Procurement activity is concentrated in a few areas and buyers. The Department of Defense obligated $5.1B, making the Defense Department the dominant customer. Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing accounted for $3.5B of obligations, and Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers accounted for $1.7B. Historical obligations show a peak in FY25 at $7.4B and a prior rise from $2.1B in FY21 to $4.4B in FY23. Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing appears as a smaller market at $639K in FY2026 to date. These figures are contract obligations, and the current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. Readers should note that award-value figures in award lists and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values, while the page totals here are obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers of AmerisourceBergen Drug in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $5.1B and is the top buyer. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $639K and the Department of Justice obligated $28K. These three agencies account for the named agency obligations in FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What market sectors capture most of AmerisourceBergen Drug's federal obligations?",
        "body": "Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing captured $3.5B of obligations and is the largest market by value. Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers captured $1.7B. Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing accounted for $639K in FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
